fixed: ["Added the Anker SOLIX S5000 row (slug anker-solix-s5000, model 'SOLIX S5000'). All cells come from Anker's US pages, read 2026-11-15. https://www.ankersolix.com/s5000 gave 5,024 Wh, 4,500 W continuous / 8,000 W peak, 120 V/240 V, and 10,000 cycles. https://www.ankersolix.com/products/s5000-portable-power-station gave the L14-30R at 4,500 W, 5-20R at 2,400 W, TT-30R at 3,600 W, overload above 4,500 W, and footnote 5: 10,000 cycles 'with the battery retaining more than 60% of its original capacity'. Both pages were added to sources.", "Placed the S5000 at row 2 and kept the Apex 300 + B300K as the pick. On the page's criteria the S5000 wins on watts from one box (4,500 W vs 3,840 W). It loses on stored energy (5,024 Wh vs 5,529.6 Wh) and on capacity left at the end of its rated cycles (60% vs 80%). So the answer paragraph and the must phrases are unchanged. Added one after-section sentence in 'One box versus the headline number' saying where it wins and where it loses.", "I skipped an S5000 price. Anker's store JSON (us.ankersolix.com) showed $3,599.99, but the www.ankersolix.com product page showed $2,599.99 'Saved $1,000.00'. The renderer prints the price itself.", "Removed the DELTA Pro 3 cells.price ('Absent from EcoFlow US store search ...'), which was not a price.", "Added a 'which fits which use' row for buying the station, extra batteries and solar panels in one cart: Apex 300 + 2x B300K + 2x 500 W solar panels, 8,294.4 Wh and 1,000 W of panels, $5,499, with the token
